      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we first need to determine the perimeter of the original triangle with side lengths of 6 cm, 7 cm, and 9 cm. \n\nPerimeter of original triangle = 6 cm + 7 cm + 9 cm = 22 cm\n\nSince the new triangle is similar to the original one,the ratio of the perimeters of two similar triangles is always the same. \n\nThe ratio of the perimeters = 110 cm / 22 cm = 5\n\nSo, the length of the longest side of the new triangle will be:\n\nLongest side of new triangle = 9 cm x 5 = 45 cm \n\nThus, the length of the longest side of the new triangle is 45 cm.\n\n$\\left\\{ \\begin{array} \\\\ 6x + 7y + 9z =110 \\\\ x + 2y + 3z =26 \\\\ x + y + z =8\\\\ \\end{array} \\right.$\nThis is a system of three equations with three variables. We can solve this system to find the values of $x,y$ and $z$ to get the answer.\n\nMultiplying the second equation by 2, the third equation by 3 and combining all the equations gives:\n\n$4x + 8y + 15z =88$ (1)\n$3x + 6y + 9z =78$ (2)\n$x + 2y +3z =8$ (3)\n\nFor equation (1): (1) - (2) gives $x + 2y -6z =10$ (4)\n\nFor equation (3)- (1) gives $2x -4z =0$ (5)\n\nFrom equation (5), we get $x = z$, substitute to equation (4):\n\n$2z -6z =10$ ; $-4z =10$; $z = -5$ (Equation for z, after dividing by 2)\n\nSubstitute z=-5 into equation (3):\n\n$x + y -3 = 8$\n\nSince we know $x=z$ from equation (5), so x = -5 and y = 4\n\nSo the longest side = $z= -5$\n\n$\\boxed{-5}$",
